Version 1.0.3 brings the port closer to the original game's combat, scripted interactions and visual effects. The changes were checked against recovered original code and focused comparisons, while preserving the modern controls, save features, audio choices and performance safeguards added to the port.

## RedCat & Enemy Combat

- **Corrected RedCat's firing cadence:** Holding the shooting button can start the next shot after the original 80% animation handoff, instead of waiting for the entire animation or a separate weapon timer. Projectiles leave the hand strictly after the original 46% release point. The intentional BIG BENG charging correction remains.
- **Matched projectile update order:** Player shots and enemy projectiles now accelerate, apply gravity and cap their velocity in the recovered order before moving. Witch homing updates after surviving movement and contact. Curved projectile paths check successive movement segments rather than cutting across the curve; saved partial steps and smooth high-refresh movement remain supported.
- **Corrected plant and gargoyle pauses between salvos:** They finish the shooting action, enter their waiting state, start its timer on the following controller check and resume only after its deadline. Remembered targets, committed salvos and interruption by selected hurt reactions follow the recovered behavior. Existing and older saved cooldowns remain supported.
- **Restored native projectile random sampling:** Enemy spread and lifetime now use the original biased random mapping and millisecond truncation. The port retains its saved per-enemy random state; projectiles already present in a save keep their existing flight parameters.
- **Restored dry landing sounds and hard-fall damage:** Ground contact uses the original dry landing sound and confirmed liquid-contact sound, with volume based on impact speed. Ordinary jumps cause no fall damage; impacts above the recovered threshold apply the original proportional damage. No-clip, cutscene and respawn protections remain.
- **Completed the dormant animation-hint API:** The original hint range, restart/clear behavior and special falling hint are supported and saved. The shipped campaign does not call this API, so this is compatibility coverage rather than a newly added player action.

## Buttons, Triggers & Moving Objects

- **Matched button transition phases:** Requests, start sounds, movement and completion callbacks now occur in the original order. Walking into or shooting a moving button cannot queue an unintended reversal; explicit script commands can remain pending while a button moves or is disabled.
- **Improved button reset and save handling:** Reset restores the authored enabled state, use count and starting pose, including initially active buttons. Saves preserve movement phases and pending requests without replaying sounds or completion callbacks. Resetting from inside a callback can no longer dispatch the wrong on/off completion. The intentional Graveyard maze reset also clears pending requests.
- **Corrected trigger contact behavior:** Waiting, entry, occupied and exit phases now follow the original controller. Trigger counts, continuous damage and explicit script activation respect their recovered rules; non-positive limits mean unlimited use.
- **Completed moving-controller commands:** Targeted movement preserves requests while disabled, dispatches crossed markers in native order and stops at the requested target. Completed once-only animations remain at their endpoint when re-enabled. Reset restores the authored initial position, and saved callback masks prevent repeated events.
- **Preserved queued work when skipping scenes:** Skipping completes enabled pending controller actions and deferred button callbacks while leaving disabled work pending. Focused checks cover the Castle bookcases, Graveyard painting/maze and affected Caves callbacks; this is not a new complete campaign playthrough.

## Particles, Explosions & Lighting

- **Corrected Fleurifee and portal particle fades:** Secondary fairy stars and portal particles use the original separate lifetime, fade-delay and fade timers, including timer arming and byte-alpha rounding. Existing ribbon behavior, relocation, sound scheduling and skip cleanup remain intact.
- **Refined enemy death smoke and Jester teleport effects:** Smoke now follows the recovered rise, size, lifetime and billboard behavior. Jester swirls use the original radial clock, emission timing, rotation and fade order. Cleanup no longer cuts off the final particles.
- **Restored explosion light flashes:** Exploding props emit the original warm light, with the original colors, maximum radius and stepped brightness sequence. Player-shot impact lights share the corrected update clock while keeping their own colors and sizes. Their first update, inclusive final deadline and short light tail now follow the original ordering.
- **Restored optional green and electrical explosion branches:** Green effects use the original masked artwork and expanding ring. Electrical effects use original gold-spark sprites, tapered streaks, generator timing and discrete positional crackles. All shipped actors disable these optional flags, so their textures and batches load only when requested. One unused original trail bitmap is absent from both the installation and CD; its unavailable visual is documented and omitted rather than replaced with invented artwork.
- **Kept effect processing bounded:** Shared render batches, cached light records, fixed visual steps, limited catch-up work and existing world-light budgets remain. The optional effects add no texture uploads or idle particle simulation to ordinary campaign levels.

## Save Continuity & Script Compatibility

- **Preserved live prop fragments in saves:** Crate, gravestone, door and other fragments retain positions, velocities, orientation, collisions and fade state instead of replaying their old trajectory against the restored world. Empty fragment groups stay empty; older saves use bounded reconstruction.
- **Preserved effect clocks:** New saves retain the corrected fairy/portal, Jester, explosion-light, impact-light and optional electrical-effect state without restarting effects or repeating old sounds. Invalid or legacy state uses validated, bounded fallback behavior.
- **Completed missing Davi-Script operators:** Added the ten previously missing unary operations, including hyperbolic/trigonometric functions and original byte-based string length, case and character conversions. These operators are declared language features but are unused by the shipped campaign.
- **Matched native number and string conversions:** Script formatting now follows the original two-stage decimal rounding and scientific notation. Parsing, signed-zero handling, integer overflow, Windows-1252 ordering and large-quotient remainder behavior were corrected against original machine-code comparisons.

## Research, Verification & Release Scope

- **Recorded each native correction separately:** The [initial original-code comparison](docs/original-source-comparison-2026-10-26.md) and [continued behavior comparison](docs/native-behavior-followup-2026-10-26.md) document evidence, implementation changes, preserved choices and remaining limits. Retained probes and focused results accompany the source.
- **Compared focused behavior with the original executable:** Evidence includes 1,332 script-conversion/arithmetic comparisons, 90 additional formatting boundaries, button-controller traces, 74 light-clock samples, death-smoke/Jester measurements, electrical-spark motion and hardware-WebGL rendering checks. Test groups overlap and are not presented as a single full-game certification.
- **Preserved intentional departures:** Modern mouse, touch and controller input, camera protection, cheats, automatic/recovery saves, player profiles, import/export, maze recovery, earned-ability fixes, protected cutscenes, enhanced torches, audio scheduling/ranges and bounded streaming/navigation remain.
- **Updated version information to 1.0.3:** The menu and desktop metadata agree. The Android source uses version name 1.0.3 and version code 5; no APK/AAB is included in this release.
- **Desktop downloads cover all six existing targets:** Linux, Windows and macOS packages are provided for x64 and ARM64, with ZIP archives and SHA-256 checksums. Windows packages are unsigned; macOS bundles built on Linux are unsigned and not notarized.
- **Built packages are not runtime-tested in this release pass:** Packages are built, archived and uploaded under the same build-only policy as 1.0.2. Uploaded file sizes and checksums are verified separately. Focused source/native comparisons do not establish a new complete campaign run, all-device validation or universal behavioral equivalence.
- These notes cover changes after the **1.0.2 release commit, `59d6298a`**. Earlier features such as the original menu, Help and save import/export remain included and are not counted again as new features.
